/">Karan Manral</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133065093,imgsize-87905.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Sharks fitted with sensors could help scientists improve hurricane forecasts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133063381.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Sharks are being used as mobile ocean sensors by University of Delaware researchers in a new study that could help improve hurricane forecasts. Electronic tags attached to sharks collect water temperature, salinity and depth data as the animals move through the Atlantic. Scientists hope the information will improve understanding of ocean conditions that influence hurricane intensity.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/us-scientists-are-tagging-sharks-with-ocean-sensors-every-time-they-surface-data-is-sent-by-satellite-to-help-forecast-how-strongly-hurricanes-may-intensify/articleshow/133063381.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/us-scientists-are-tagging-sharks-with-ocean-sensors-every-time-they-surface-data-is-sent-by-satellite-to-help-forecast-how-strongly-hurricanes-may-intensify/articleshow/133063381.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T13:45:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133063945,imgsize-95387.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Budapest’s low Danube exposes two German soldiers and a DKW motorcycle buried for 80 years]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133062997.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Unusually low water levels in Budapest’s Danube River have exposed Second World War remains hidden for around 80 years. Recovery teams found the bodies of two Wehrmacht soldiers, their well-preserved identity discs, a German military motorbike, anti-tank mines and other wartime objects near Batthyány Square. The finds could help identify the soldiers and reveal more about Budapest’s final wartime days.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/budapests-low-danube-exposed-two-german-soldiers-and-a-dkw-military-motorcycle-mud-mixed-with-gas-oil-preserved-identity-discs-after-around-80-years/articleshow/133062997.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/budapests-low-danube-exposed-two-german-soldiers-and-a-dkw-military-motorcycle-mud-mixed-with-gas-oil-preserved-identity-discs-after-around-80-years/articleshow/133062997.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133063309,imgsize-235763.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Punch thrives after virality: Once-orphaned macaque turns 1]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133063727.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Punch, the orphaned Japanese macaque, joyously celebrated his first birthday, receiving heartfelt greetings from around the world. Now a part of a vibrant troop, he enjoys playful interactions and grooming sessions with fellow macaques. Generous donations funded significant upgrades to his enclosure, including plush toys from IKEA, and millions in contributions are set to enhance all macaque habitats, particularly to tackle welfare issues during Japan's sweltering summers.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/punch-the-baby-monkey-turns-1-he-is-making-friends-and-his-enclosure-is-getting-an-upgrade/articleshow/133063727.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/punch-the-baby-monkey-turns-1-he-is-making-friends-and-his-enclosure-is-getting-an-upgrade/articleshow/133063727.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T12:45:51+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133063768,imgsize-212562.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How 10 billion trees transformed South Korea's post-war forests]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133063421.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-korea-planted-more-than-10-billion-trees-after-the-korean-war-and-its-forests-made-a-remarkable-comeback/articleshow/133063421.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/south-korea-planted-more-than-10-billion-trees-after-the-korean-war-and-its-forests-made-a-remarkable-comeback/articleshow/133063421.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T12:25:19+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133063421,imgsize-296162.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Biologists tagged an 87-pound paddlefish in 2007; 18 years later, the fish weighed 98 pounds]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133032647.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An impressive paddlefish, initially tagged in 2007, made headlines when an angler recaught it after an astonishing eighteen years. This ancient species revealed invaluable long-term growth data to scientists, adding eleven pounds and increasing its length by three inches. Such recaptures are pivotal, offering critical insights into fish survival and migration, underscoring the necessity of sustained fish tagging initiatives for conservation efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-north-dakota-biologists-tagged-an-87-pound-paddlefish-18-years-later-an-angler-caught-the-same-fish-weighing-98-pounds/articleshow/133032647.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2007-north-dakota-biologists-tagged-an-87-pound-paddlefish-18-years-later-an-angler-caught-the-same-fish-weighing-98-pounds/articleshow/133032647.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T12:01:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133032752,imgsize-84322.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Houthi attack suspected at Saudi gas facility in Jubail; Aramco Jazan fire extinguished]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133063118.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/houthi-attack-suspected-at-saudi-gas-facility-in-jubail-aramco-jazan-fire-extinguished/articleshow/133063118.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/houthi-attack-suspected-at-saudi-gas-facility-in-jubail-aramco-jazan-fire-extinguished/articleshow/133063118.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T11:41:55+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kanchan Yadav</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133063170,imgsize-109209.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists bred 39 surviving clams in Florida’s Indian River Lagoon; they have since outplanted 65 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133030865.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Florida's Indian River Lagoon shows signs of recovery after decades of environmental decline.  Scientists are restoring critical habitats like reefs, shellfish beds, seagrass, and wetlands.  Efforts focus on reintroducing clams, which were nearly extinct due to overharvesting and algal blooms.  Millions of juvenile and adult "super clams" have been released into the lagoon.  Local governments are addressing runoff issues to support the lagoon's ongoing restoration.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2018-scientists-found-just-39-surviving-clams-in-floridas-indian-river-lagoon-they-bred-them-and-have-since-outplanted-65-million/articleshow/133030865.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-2018-scientists-found-just-39-surviving-clams-in-floridas-indian-river-lagoon-they-bred-them-and-have-since-outplanted-65-million/articleshow/133030865.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T10:38:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133031022,imgsize-144433.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Palau removed invasive rats; a year later, fish biomass rose 183% and leaf nitrogen jumped 80%]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133025730.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A new study from Ulong Island in Palau has found the first experimental evidence that restoring seabird populations by removing invasive rats can also help nearby coral reefs recover. Within a year, researchers recorded more seabirds, increased nutrient movement from land to sea and higher fish biomass, showing that island restoration can benefit both terrestrial and marine ecosystems.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2024-palau-removed-invasive-rats-from-ulong-island-one-year-later-fish-biomass-rose-183-and-leaf-nitrogen-increased-about-80-at-one-reef-site/articleshow/133025730.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/in-2024-palau-removed-invasive-rats-from-ulong-island-one-year-later-fish-biomass-rose-183-and-leaf-nitrogen-increased-about-80-at-one-reef-site/articleshow/133025730.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T09:29:20+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133027080,imgsize-90875.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Britain is dropping 20 concrete reef cubes and 44 tons of scallop shells into the sea to bring back native oysters]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133027146.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Engineered concrete cubes are being deployed in Britain's North Sea to restore native oyster populations. These structures provide a stable foundation for oysters and habitat for marine life. The project aims to rebuild a collapsed ecosystem after a significant decline in oyster numbers. Volunteers are actively involved in cleaning and attaching oysters to the reef cubes.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/britain-is-dropping-20-concrete-reef-cubes-and-44-tons-of-scallop-shells-into-the-sea-in-the-hope-to-bring-back-its-native-oysters-who-have-reduced-by-95-since-1800s/articleshow/133027146.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/britain-is-dropping-20-concrete-reef-cubes-and-44-tons-of-scallop-shells-into-the-sea-in-the-hope-to-bring-back-its-native-oysters-who-have-reduced-by-95-since-1800s/articleshow/133027146.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T09:29:13+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133027386,imgsize-103915.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Four killed after helicopter crashes on steep hillside in Rio de Janeiro]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133061331.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/four-killed-in-helicopter-crash-in-rio-de-janeiro/articleshow/133061331.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/four-killed-in-helicopter-crash-in-rio-de-janeiro/articleshow/133061331.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T07:07:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133061342,imgsize-255180.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Strait of Hormuz standoff: What Iran, US want and what it takes to reopen waterway]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133061432.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/strait-of-hormuz-standoff-what-iran-us-want-and-what-it-takes-to-reopen-waterway/articleshow/133061432.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/strait-of-hormuz-standoff-what-iran-us-want-and-what-it-takes-to-reopen-waterway/articleshow/133061432.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T07:59:02+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133061504,imgsize-99478.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pentagon asks defence firms to ramp up weapons production as Iran war drains stockpile: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133061658.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/defence/international/pentagon-asks-defence-firms-to-ramp-up-weapons-production-as-iran-war-drains-stockpile-report/articleshow/133061658.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/defence/international/pentagon-asks-defence-firms-to-ramp-up-weapons-production-as-iran-war-drains-stockpile-report/articleshow/133061658.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T09:02:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Ayush Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133061847,imgsize-116086.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Colombia rocked by car bomb blast a day after new President takes charge]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133061382.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In southwestern Colombia, a car bomb detonated at a toll plaza on Saturday, just a day after Abelardo de la Espriella took office as president. The army promptly attributed the incident to dissident FARC factions, leaving two security guards injured. In response, President de la Espriella issued a stern warning to armed groups, urging them to comply with the rule of law.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/colombia-rocked-by-car-bomb-blast-a-day-after-new-president-abelardo-de-la-espriella-takes-charge/articleshow/133061382.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/colombia-rocked-by-car-bomb-blast-a-day-after-new-president-abelardo-de-la-espriella-takes-charge/articleshow/133061382.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-09T07:28:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://pu